# Game folders contain custom binary-ish data formats (Run 3's level/terrain
# data in particular is a dense custom encoding, not plain text) that must
# never be touched by git's line-ending normalization. Without this, Windows
# git (core.autocrlf=true) silently converts CRLF -> LF while staging files,
# which corrupted Run3Source's text/*.txt level data (confirmed: every line
# lost exactly 1 byte, matching the file's line count exactly) and caused
# the compiled game to crash with "An unknown error occurred."
Run3Source/** -text
2048/** -text
AlienShooter/** -text
